The junk/not-junk half of the report suites owns this message, on both the JMAP
and the IMAP side.

Its own message in its own mailbox, for the reason 08-jmap-state.eml gives: a
report *files* the message, and on JMAP that replaces the Email's mailboxIds, so
reporting a COPY of a shared fixture would drag the baseline out of the
count-asserted INBOX and Archive.

It is separate from 11-report-phishing.eml because the two report tests run
concurrently — cargo runs the tests in one binary in parallel, and CI passes no
`--test-threads=1`. Sharing one message let each test observe the other's
keywords, which is a failure that only ever appears on the runner.
